.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/flat-cache Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "flat-cache"
.PP
.RS 4
A stupidly simple key/value storage using files to persist the data 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP
.SH "install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm i \-\-save flat\-cache
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const flatCache = require('flat\-cache');
// loads the cache, if one does not exists for the given
// Id a new one will be prepared to be created
const cache = flatCache\&.load('cacheId');

// sets a key on the cache
cache\&.setKey('key', { foo: 'var' });

// get a key from the cache
cache\&.getKey('key'); // { foo: 'var' }

// fetch the entire persisted object
cache\&.all(); // { 'key': { foo: 'var' } }

// remove a key
cache\&.removeKey('key'); // removes a key from the cache

// save it to disk
cache\&.save(); // very important, if you don't save no changes will be persisted\&.
// cache\&.save( true /* noPrune */) // can be used to prevent the removal of non visited keys

// loads the cache from a given directory, if one does
// not exists for the given Id a new one will be prepared to be created
const cache = flatCache\&.load('cacheId', path\&.resolve('\&./path/to/folder'));

// The following methods are useful to clear the cache
// delete a given cache
flatCache\&.clearCacheById('cacheId'); // removes the cacheId document if one exists\&.

// delete all cache
flatCache\&.clearAll(); // remove the cache directory
.fi
.PP
.SH "Motivation for this module"
.PP
I needed a super simple and dumb \fBin-memory cache\fP with optional disk persistance in order to make a script that will beutify files with \fResformatter\fP only execute on the files that were changed since the last run\&. To make that possible we need to store the \fRfileSize\fP and \fRmodificationTime\fP of the files\&. So a simple \fRkey/value\fP storage was needed and Bam! this module was born\&.
.SH "Important notes"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
If no directory is especified when the \fRload\fP method is called, a folder named \fR\&.cache\fP will be created inside the module directory when \fRcache\&.save\fP is called\&. If you're committing your \fRnode_modules\fP to any vcs, you might want to ignore the default \fR\&.cache\fP folder, or specify a custom directory\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
The values set on the keys of the cache should be \fRstringify-able\fP ones, meaning no circular references
.IP "\(bu" 2
All the changes to the cache state are done to memory
.IP "\(bu" 2
I could have used a timer or \fRObject\&.observe\fP to deliver the changes to disk, but I wanted to keep this module intentionally dumb and simple
.IP "\(bu" 2
Non visited keys are removed when \fRcache\&.save()\fP is called\&. If this is not desired, you can pass \fRtrue\fP to the save call like: \fRcache\&.save( true /* noPrune */ )\fP\&.
.PP
